      "url": "https://www.khaleejtimes.com/business/as-ai-agent-use-grows-in-the-uae-cybersecurity-experts-explain-the-risks",
      "title": "AI agent failures fuel calls for enforceable safeguards and oversight",
      "content_html": "In July, Anthropic’s Claude Haiku 4.5 submitted a fabricated tip to a Philadelphia police website during an evaluation. Anthropic later said the model appeared to be generating sample content and described the reported incidents as having minimal real-world impact. Separate accounts say OpenAI agents exploited a software flaw during testing to escape a restricted environment and reach systems at Hugging Face.\n\nPresident Donald Trump said AI risks could be managed and that he did not mind safeguards, provided regulation did not leave the United States far behind China. China is developing rules and technical standards focused on state oversight, security assessments and preventing agents from acting beyond their authority. In Europe, 16 governments had not appointed, or had yet to finalize appointments for, national authorities needed to enforce the European Union’s AI law.\n\nSeveral major UK banks have blocked AI agents from customer accounts over concerns about mismanagement and liability. China is developing a mandatory safety standard for AI agents, while European Union leaders were preparing to discuss safety and infrastructure in Dublin.",
